shared/sh_portal.qc
shared/sh_strafe.qc
// Patch 378: sampled-motion interpolation, one speller for cl_watch.qc and the
// body stream.  Pure functions; anywhere before cl_watch.qc would do.
shared/sh_interp.qc

// BUILD 24.  The same file menu.dat compiles, not a copy -- the replay chrome
// and the +showscores board want the list views, the sliders and the hit
// testing the map browser already runs on.  Its one #ifdef MENU block stays
// menu-only (cl_defs.qc already declares the IE_* constants); see the note
// beside the printf define at the top of it.  Here rather than lower down
// because cl_hud.qc and everything after it may draw with it.
sui_sys.qc

client/cl_board.qc
client/cl_keys.qc
// AFTER cl_keys.qc and BEFORE cl_hud.qc.  Build 30.  The HUD keeps reporting the
// BODY while the camera is off flying, so it reads rec_gh_on and rec_gh_bodyorg --
// and a QC global has to exist before the file that reads it, which is the same
// ordering constraint the two declaration blocks at the top of cl_keys.qc are
// there for.
client/cl_ghost.qc
client/cl_decals.qc
// AFTER cl_decals.qc only by convention -- the two are independent walks of the
// same entity lump and neither reads the other.  Before cl_main.qc, which calls
// Sprite_LoadFromWorld from CSQC_WorldLoaded and Sprite_Draw from UpdateView.
client/cl_sprites.qc
// Source fog (env_fog_controller / sky_camera): a third independent walk of the
// same lump, reading nothing from the other two.  It has to sit BEFORE
// cl_gfx.qc, which greys the "Map fog" row out using vbsp_fog_count, and before
// cl_main.qc, which calls Fog_LoadFromWorld from CSQC_WorldLoaded and Fog_Frame
// from CSQC_UpdateView.  It needs nothing from anyone, so this is early enough.
client/cl_fog.qc
// Build 49.  A FOURTH independent walk of the same entity lump -- the decals,
// the sprites and the fog are the other three, and no one of the four reads
// another.  It has to sit BEFORE cl_gfx.qc, which greys the "Map particles"
// row out using em_seen, and before cl_main.qc, which calls Emit_RegisterCvars
// from CSQC_Init, Emit_LoadFromWorld from CSQC_WorldLoaded and Emit_Frame from
// CSQC_UpdateView.  Like cl_fog.qc it needs nothing from anyone, so beside its
// three siblings is early enough.
client/cl_emit.qc
// Build 66.  A FIFTH independent walk of the same entity lump -- the decals,
// sprites, fog and emitters are the other four, and no one of the five reads
// another.  env_soundscape: the entity Source maps actually use for ambience,
// and the reason a Momentum map currently sounds identical in every room.
//
// It needs nothing from anyone (getentitytoken, fopen, sound/soundupdate and
// traceline are all engine builtins), so beside its four siblings is early
// enough.  It must sit BEFORE cl_main.qc, which calls Snds_RegisterCvars from
// CSQC_Init, Snds_LoadFromWorld from CSQC_WorldLoaded, Snds_Frame from
// CSQC_UpdateView and Snds_ConsoleCommand from CSQC_ConsoleCommand.
client/cl_soundscape.qc
// Patch 335, Phase 1 of playing on the client.  A SIXTH independent walk of
// the entity lump: the client-side mirror of the stateless Source triggers
// (teleport, push, setspeed), fired from inside client prediction through the
// CSQC_PredictPlayerMove hook so a booster or a stage reset no longer costs a
// round trip.  It needs nothing from anyone (getentitytoken, tracebox and the
// predmove_* globals are all engine-provided), so beside its five siblings is
// early enough, and it must sit BEFORE cl_main.qc, which calls
// Trig_RegisterCvars from CSQC_Init, Trig_LoadForMap from CSQC_WorldLoaded,
// Trig_Frame from CSQC_UpdateView and Trig_ConsoleCommand from
// CSQC_ConsoleCommand.
client/cl_triggers.qc
client/cl_hud.qc
// AFTER cl_hud.qc, which owns HUD_Text/HUD_TextR, ui_cv_scale and ui_font_ui.
// Patch 270: the lobby network monitor -- the on-screen replacement for
// counting `cl_shownet 3` lines by eye.  It needs nothing from anything below.
client/cl_netmon.qc
// Build 65: the Boarding window.  AFTER cl_hud.qc for HUD_Text*, HUD_Size,
// HUD_Rect, HUD_EnergyRef, Board_Alpha's callers and the font globals, and AFTER
// cl_board.qc (line 20) for board_* / leave_* / seg_live_*.  It must also sit
// BEFORE cl_hudedit.qc, which lists it as a draggable element, and before
// cl_main.qc, which calls Boarding_RegisterCvars from CSQC_Init and
// Boarding_Draw from the HUD stack.  Beside cl_netmon.qc satisfies all four and
// is the same slot that file documents for the same reason.
client/cl_boarding.qc
client/cl_timer.qc
client/cl_saveloc.qc
client/cl_gfx.qc
// Patch 372: the vote box.  After cl_gfx.qc (Gfx_Row, Gfx_Field) and cl_hud.qc
// (HUD_SK, the map clock); cl_hudedit.qc and cl_main.qc call into it.
client/cl_vote.qc
client/cl_replay.qc
client/cl_zones.qc
// AFTER cl_zones.qc: the path is drawn with Zone_Line, and before cl_main.qc,
// which calls into it from CSQC_UpdateView and CSQC_InputEvent.
client/cl_watch.qc
// BEFORE cl_scores.qc, which is the only thing that will read it -- the ONLINE
// half of the leaderboard: one GET against surfd's /api/board, parsed and kept.
//
// It needs sh_json.qc for the parser and sh_time.qc for Time_TickString, both
// of which are at the top of this file already, and NOTHING ELSE -- it draws
// nothing and touches no HUD state.  That is why it can sit this early, and it
// is also the point: the request path is testable from a config
// (`board_fetch`, `board_status`) before a single tab consumes it, so a change
// to the tabs cannot break the network path by accident.
//
// It declares CSQC's one and only URI_Get_Callback.  The engine finds that by
// NAME (pr_bgcmd.c:6003) and there can be exactly one per VM, so anything else
// in csprogs that ever wants uri_get has to branch inside it rather than
// declare its own -- the same constraint m_lobby.qc documents for the menu.
client/cl_online.qc
// Patch 340, player customization.  Three files, one direction of dependency:
// cl_chat (the CSQC_Parse_Print hook, the ring, the silence list) needs nothing
// but sh_font; cl_avatar (the `hud_player` customizer, the palette mirror,
// UIC_AVATAR) needs cl_hud's cursor register and the panel flags; cl_players
// (the room list) needs the palette from cl_avatar and the silence list and
// colour rule from cl_chat -- and cl_scores calls INTO it (Players_Panel runs
// inside the board's sui bracket, because a second bracket in a frame draws
// dead buttons), so all three sit before cl_scores.qc and after everything
// they read.
client/cl_chat.qc
client/cl_avatar.qc
client/cl_players.qc
// AFTER cl_watch.qc, because clicking a row hands the file straight to
// Watch_Open, and after cl_timer.qc because every time on it is formatted at
// Timer_Tick's rate.  Stage 2 of build 24.
client/cl_scores.qc
client/cl_portal.qc
// AFTER cl_scores.qc, which owns Scores_LastOf -- the rank scan parses the same
// <ticks>_<tag> filenames the leaderboard does and there is no second copy of
// that parser.  Also after cl_timer.qc, whose ui_sp_* rows ARE the card's split
// table and whose Timer_SplitsClass draws the same marks in both places, and
// after cl_hud.qc for HUD_Text and the rect registry.  Build 48.
client/cl_results.qc
// AFTER cl_results.qc and cl_scores.qc, and before cl_hudedit.qc.  Build 57,
// Stage T: the lobby time store -- the client half of "a lobby saves your times
// on your own PC", because a lobby server keeps nothing and could not write to
// this disk if it wanted to.
//
// It needs Scores_LastOf from cl_scores.qc (the <ticks>_<tag> filename parse is
// the leaderboard's and there is no second copy of it), Results_LegName from
// cl_results.qc so a print names the leg the card names, and Timer_Tick from
// cl_timer.qc to format a time.  cl_results.qc in turn asks it for the lobby best
// a finish was measured against -- the server zeroes TIMERPBWAS in a lobby -- so
// that ONE function is forward-declared there, the same arrangement sv_zones.qc
// has with the timer's SV_TimerChatLeg.  Nothing below this line is needed by it.
client/cl_lobbytime.qc
// Patch 361: the completion banner.  After cl_lobbytime.qc (LT_BestOnLegC) and
// cl_results.qc (Results_KeyRank / Results_Rank, and the toast it replaces).
client/cl_banner.qc
// LAST BEFORE cl_main.qc.  Build 31.  The layout editor refuses to share the
// screen with a replay, the leaderboard or the results card, so it needs
// rec_wt_open (cl_watch.qc) and ui_rs_cursor (cl_results.qc); it also consumes
// the rect registry, which has to live in cl_hud.qc because every drawer calls
// into it.  After all of them is the only position that satisfies both, and it
// needs nothing from cl_main.qc.
//
// BUILD 48 took rec_sb_open OUT of that list -- it is declared in cl_hud.qc now,
// because cl_watch.qc compiles before cl_scores.qc and could not otherwise test
// it before releasing the cursor.  See the block beside ui_he_open there.
client/cl_hudedit.qc
// LAST, after cl_hudedit.qc.  Build 54: the trigger/entity inspector.
//
// It needs Sprite_ParseVec from cl_sprites.qc, Zone_Line/Zone_Face from
// cl_zones.qc to draw a volume, and HUD_Text from cl_hud.qc -- but the binding
// constraint is the CURSOR.  Releasing it means testing every other owner, and
// the last of those to be declared is ui_he_open's neighbour in cl_hudedit.qc.
// Its own flag, ui_ev_cursor, is declared in cl_entview.qc itself: nothing that
// compiles earlier reads it (cl_hudedit.qc does not test it -- the claim
// register in cl_hud.qc absorbs the overlap), and its two readers, this file and
// cl_main.qc, both follow.  Move it up only if an earlier file ever needs it.
client/cl_entview.qc
client/cl_main.qc
